I think that this should be in the FAQ

Around level 3 there are _two_ sets of steps leading down. One set
leads to the gnomish mines. The gnomish mines go down several levels,
with gnome town a few levels from the bottom.  The mines end around
level 12.  The bottom of the mines has a special treasure if you know
where to look.  After that, your only choice is to go back up to the
level where you entered the mines and take the second stairway, and
continue down the dungeon.

You will instantly know whether the stair way you took was to the
mines or not, because there is no organization to the mine layout: no
neat rooms with connecting passages (no passages '##' at all actually,
until some @#%$#@ dwarf with a pick-axe starts hammering) and no
complex mazes.  Just a bunch of wide open and narrow spaces and walls.
There are also many dwarves and gnomes.

The actual levels at which everything appears varies from game to
game.

